with_skill.response:
Reading the Customer.io Liquid skill to get the exact object and relationship syntax.

Here's the correct syntax for each case in an **object-triggered** campaign:

## 1. The triggering subscription's attributes

```liquid
{{trigger.subscription.plan_name}}
{{trigger.subscription.renewal_date}}
```

Object-triggered workflows use the **singular** slug (`subscription`) under `trigger.` for the object that fired it.

## 2. The recipient's relationship attributes to that subscription

```liquid
{{customer._relationship.started_at}}
{{customer._relationship.status}}
```

Note the **underscore** — it's `customer._relationship`, not `trigger.relationship`. The recipient is always `{{customer}}`, and their relationship attributes to the triggering object are under `{{customer._relationship.<attr>}}`.

## 3. A list of the recipient's other active subscriptions

```liquid
{% for sub in objects.subscriptions %}
  {% if sub.object_id != trigger.subscription.object_id and sub.status == "active" %}
    {{sub.plan_name}} — renews {{sub.renewal_date | date: "%B %d, %Y"}}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
```

General object access uses the **plural** slug (`subscriptions`) under `objects.`. Each profile can have **at most 10 objects of the same type** — `[0]` is the most recently created, `[9]` the oldest, and an 11th never renders. The triggering subscription is **not necessarily** `[0]`.

## Complete example with fallbacks

```liquid
{% comment %}latest liquid — version-check by hovering "last saved" in the message editor{% endcomment %}

Hi {{customer.first_name | default: "there"}},

Your {{trigger.subscription.plan_name | default: "subscription"}} 
{% if trigger.subscription.renewal_date %}renews on {{trigger.subscription.renewal_date | date: "%B %d, %Y"}}{% endif %}.

{% if customer._relationship.status %}
  Your subscription status: {{customer._relationship.status}}
{% endif %}

{% comment %}other active subscriptions{% endcomment %}
{% assign other_subs = "" %}
{% for sub in objects.subscriptions %}
  {% if sub.object_id != trigger.subscription.object_id and sub.status == "active" %}
    {% assign other_subs = "found" %}
    • {{sub.plan_name | default: "Subscription"}} — renews {{sub.renewal_date | date: "%B %d, %Y"}}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if other_subs == "" %}
  You have no other active subscriptions.
{% endif %}
```

## Key warnings

**Missing data fails the send in Customer.io** — always add fallbacks with `| default:` (latest Liquid) or `{% if x != blank %}` (legacy). Verify by previewing against a profile **with** and **without** each attribute.

**Namespace matters:** `{{trigger.subscriptions}}` (plural) renders **empty with no error** and the message sends — wrong namespace is the silent failure mode. Object triggers use singular under `trigger.`, plural under `objects.`.

**Liquid version assumed:** The code above uses `| default:`, which is **latest Liquid only** (accounts created Nov 28, 2023 or later, or all Design Studio messages). Check your message's version by hovering the "last saved" date in the editor. For **legacy** Liquid, replace `| default: "..."` with `{% if x != blank %}{{x}}{% else %}...{% endif %}`.

